      "strengths_deep_dive": [
        "IMANA demonstrates substantial institutional longevity, delivering direct medical care since its founding in 1967. The organization achieved <cite id=\"1\">a 96 out of 100 overall score on Charity Navigator</cite>, supported by high marks in leadership and governance culture. In FY2024, IMANA generated <cite id=\"3\">$3,675,972 in revenue</cite>, reflecting steady growth from prior fiscal years with <cite id=\"3\">a 3-year revenue CAGR of 43.4%</cite>.\n\nFinancial resilience is a core pillar of the organization's structure. IMANA holds <cite id=\"1\">33.0 months of working capital in reserve</cite>, protecting operational continuity against economic fluctuations. The organization also maintains peak operational transparency, holding <cite id=\"1\">a Platinum Seal of Transparency from Candid</cite> while fulfilling direct medical services globally."
      ],
      "summary": "Founded in 1967, the Islamic Medical Association of North America (IMANA) provides direct medical relief and global health assistance <cite id=\"1\">with over 50 years of operating history</cite>. In FY2024, the charity managed <cite id=\"3\">$3,675,972 in total revenue</cite> to execute direct patient care programs including medical relief missions in regions like Jordan, Bangladesh, and Pakistan <cite id=\"6\">through international medical initiatives</cite>.\n\nIMANA's operational structure balances direct medical aid delivery with strategic grantmaking to foreign and domestic healthcare partners. The organization maintains <cite id=\"1\">a four-star Charity Navigator rating with a 96 out of 100 overall score</cite>, supported by strong working capital reserves. With <cite id=\"3\">a 76.5% program expense ratio in FY2024</cite>, spending slightly exceeds the 75% sector benchmark. While IMANA holds <cite id=\"1\">high transparency credentials including a Candid Platinum Seal</cite>, board governance tracking remains an area for improvement. The charity provides clear pathways for faith-based giving, offering <cite id=\"2\">verified zakat-eligible relief initiatives</cite> serving vulnerable populations globally.",
